# EXPECTATION FOR LANE RUN 24 — derived and committed ALONE, BEFORE the run (D0A-R21-07).
#
# Target commit: f61d8df. The instrument changes — the negative-control fixture, the extracted
# `observe_assembly`, and the verifier's requirement that runs from 24 on carry the negative
# control's evidence — were committed at 1c5f92b and f61d8df, before this file.
#
# =========================================================================================
# THE DERIVATION
# =========================================================================================
#
# Run 23 measured root 224 / 6 / 230 at b51bd8f. TWO identities added since, none removed:
#
#   the_topology_fixture_leaves_the_parents_process_group          | b1_integration | FEATURE
#   the_control_reports_topology_when_the_daemons_child_leaves...   | b1_integration | FEATURE
#
# **Both gate on the FEATURE FIRST** — verified by grep of the first gate after each `fn`, not
# from memory — so in the lane's FEATURELESS build they skip at root exactly as they do
# unprivileged. The executed count therefore does NOT move:
#
#   EXECUTED  224 + 0 = 224
#   SKIPPED     6 + 2 =   8
#   reported  230 + 2 = 232       (agrees with the measured unprivileged 204/28/232)
#
# Cross-check: unprivileged went 204/26/230 -> 204/28/232, i.e. +0 executed and +2 skipped —
# the same partition of the same two tests. Any other root figure falsifies one of these.
#
# **A skipped test is scored as a pass by libtest, which is why the skip count is predicted
# rather than ignored.** Eight skips is the largest this lane has carried; each must still quote
# its own blocker in the transcript.
#
# =========================================================================================
# RUN 24 HAS THREE PARTS, AND THE THIRD IS ITS REASON
# =========================================================================================
#
# PART A   — the standard 17-target lane, featureless. Count evidence, comparable to run 23.
# PART B1  — the POSITIVE control, feature-built, at root.
# PART B2  — the NEGATIVE control, feature-built, at root. New this run.
#
# Only Part A contributes to the counts above.
#
# =========================================================================================
# WHAT EACH NEGATIVE-CONTROL OUTCOME MEANS — this is the run's reason
# =========================================================================================
#
# The fixture makes the daemon's AI call `setpgid(0,0)` and then `exec` the real stubborn AI.
# `exec` replaces the image in the SAME process, so `ppid` still points at the daemon: the
# child is VERIFIED as the daemon's own and OUTSIDE its group — precisely `Topology`'s input.
#
# 1. **`Topology`.** The control detects a topology defect **it would otherwise have passed**.
#    This is what gives the three prior `Reached` verdicts their meaning: a control that can
#    discriminate, having said `Reached` three times, is reporting something. Expected outcome,
#    and the least informative of the three in isolation — its value is retrospective.
#
# 2. **`Reached`.** THE CONTROL CANNOT DETECT A TOPOLOGY DEFECT. Then every `Reached` in the
#    record is consistent with a control that never discriminated, and **the supplementary scan
#    is WITHDRAWN from D0A-R28-02's row entirely — not weakened.** The row would keep
#    `killed == false` and the daemon's self-report, which is the §4 boundedness closure and
#    does not depend on the scan. **This is the outcome worth more than the expected one**, and
#    the consequence is fixed here so it cannot be renegotiated after the fact.
#
# 3. **`Scan` or `Unresolved`.** The fixture did not produce the input it claims — a finding
#    about the FIXTURE, not about the control or the product. The mechanism is already proven
#    unprivileged (`the_topology_fixture_leaves_the_parents_process_group`, RED-proven), so
#    this would mean something about the assembly path differs from the direct-spawn path, and
#    that difference is the finding.
#
# The verifier REFUSES the run for any of 2 or 3. A run whose negative control does not return
# `Topology` is not an accepted run: the lane's evidence would not support the closure it is
# cited for, and "the run was properly conducted" must not certify "the product passed".
#
# =========================================================================================
# THE POSITIVE CONTROL'S FOURTH `Reached` PROVES NOTHING NEW ON ITS OWN
# =========================================================================================
#
# Stated before the run so a fourth green cannot read as accumulating confidence. Runs 20, 21
# and 23 all returned `Reached`; run 23's was the first under the enforced provenance gate.
# A fourth adds one more instance of the outcome that changes nothing.
#
# **It is the NEGATIVE control that gives the prior greens their meaning, or removes it.**
# Three confirmations and zero discriminations is `DEFECT_CLASSES` 49's silence; the discriminating
# observation is the only one that resolves it, and it has never run.
#
# =========================================================================================
# THE VERIFIER DECIDES ACCEPTANCE, AND THE COMMIT BINDING IS CAPTURED FOR THE FIRST TIME
# =========================================================================================
#
# `scripts/lane-accept.py scratch/lane-run-24` runs LAST. **If it refuses, the run is not
# accepted regardless of what the counts say.**
#
# **Run 23's commit was established by INFERENCE FROM TIMESTAMPS** — b51bd8f committed at 13:10,
# the transcript stamped 13:16, no commit between. Better than memory, weaker than a binding,
# and its record says so. Run 24 is the first where `hygiene.txt` carries `git rev-parse HEAD`
# and `git status --porcelain` written BY THE RUN, and the verifier refuses a run whose tree was
# DIRTY — artifacts from a dirty tree describe no commit at all.
#
# **The limit that remains:** the verifier checks that a commit was recorded and the tree was
# clean. It does not check that the recorded commit is the one being merged. That is still a
# human's job, and an ACCEPTED verdict does not do it.
EXPECTED_EXECUTED=224
EXPECTED_SKIPPED=8
EXPECTED_REPORTED=232
